From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] albumart: also find folder.jpg, front.jpg, AlbumArt.jpg

find_stream_art() only tries cover.png, cover.jpg and cover.webp.  Folder
images from Windows Media Player, many rippers and older players are named
folder.jpg, front.jpg or AlbumArt.jpg, so `albumart` answered "No file
exists" for albums that do have a folder image.  Try those names after
cover.* (cover.* keeps priority).  A found image is cached per directory
by LastInputStream; an album with no image costs up to nine failed open()s
per albumart request instead of three.

---
--- a/src/command/FileCommands.cxx	2026-10-24 02:07:05.207297260 +0000
+++ b/src/command/FileCommands.cxx	2026-10-24 02:07:05.218117861 +0000
@@ -134,6 +134,15 @@
 		"cover.png",
 		"cover.jpg",
 		"cover.webp",
+		/* EROS Q: names other rippers/players use for the folder
+		   image, tried after cover.*; FAT matches case-insensitively,
+		   Folder.jpg covers case-sensitive storage */
+		"folder.jpg",
+		"folder.png",
+		"front.jpg",
+		"AlbumArt.jpg",
+		"albumart.jpg",
+		"Folder.jpg",
 	};
 
 	for(const auto name : art_names) {
